<v Tom Kerrigan>like five, ten thousand a year, and that kills your yield.</v>

c21b6ccb-ea74-4225-8514-3495a0233a54/62-0
00:08:05.733 --> 00:08:06.658
<v Anh Tran (Guest)>Wow. Okay.</v>

c2468f14-d78a-4632-b5ff-cf6216fc15e3/63-0
00:08:07.074 --> 00:08:11.118
<v Tom Kerrigan>Yeah. It's one of the biggest mistakes I see interstate investors make.</v>

c2468f14-d78a-4632-b5ff-cf6216fc15e3/63-1
00:08:11.118 --> 00:08:17.183
<v Tom Kerrigan>They see a cheap house in Ipswich with a good rent, and then they get the insurance quote.</v>

8f9bacb4-efcd-4a3e-92e4-c3feb0b300b9/64-0
00:08:17.879 --> 00:08:19.740
<v Callum P (Guest)>Okay. So no flood.</v>

19c47ec4-e17e-4b02-a9c1-6580f9388430/65-0
00:08:20.759 --> 00:08:26.802
<v Tom Kerrigan>No flood, and I'll check the insurance before we offer on anything. Okay, so, the house itself.</v>

19c47ec4-e17e-4b02-a9c1-6580f9388430/65-1
00:08:26.802 --> 00:08:30.002
<v Tom Kerrigan>What are you thinking? Have you got any preferences?</v>

8f9bacb4-efcd-4a3e-92e4-c3feb0b300b9/66-0
00:08:30.807 --> 00:08:35.021
<v Callum P (Guest)>Um, so, I've been reading about, like, dual income properties. Granny flats. Duplexes.</v>

8f9bacb4-efcd-4a3e-92e4-c3feb0b300b9/66-1
00:08:35.021 --> 00:08:38.910
<v Callum P (Guest)>I thought that might be a way to get a better yield.</v>

c21b6ccb-ea74-4225-8514-3495a0233a54/67-0
00:08:39.908 --> 00:08:41.903
<v Anh Tran (Guest)>I don't know about that.</v>

8f9bacb4-efcd-4a3e-92e4-c3feb0b300b9/68-0
00:08:42.357 --> 00:08:44.146
<v Callum P (Guest)>I know, Anh's not keen.</v>

c21b6ccb-ea74-4225-8514-3495a0233a54/69-0
00:08:46.206 --> 00:08:52.881
<v Anh Tran (Guest)>I'm not not keen. I just think it's more complicated. Like, two tenants, two lots of everything.</v>

19c47ec4-e17e-4b02-a9c1-6580f9388430/70-0
00:08:53.626 --> 00:09:00.398
<v Tom Kerrigan>Yeah, it's a fair point. So, in Queensland, the rules on granny flats have loosened up a lot,</v>

19c47ec4-e17e-4b02-a9c1-6580f9388430/70-1
00:09:00.398 --> 00:09:05.664
<v Tom Kerrigan>in most places you can now rent one out to anyone, not just family,</v>

19c47ec4-e17e-4b02-a9c1-6580f9388430/70-2
00:09:05.664 --> 00:09:10.178
<v Tom Kerrigan>though it depends on the council and whether it's been approved properly.</v>

19c47ec4-e17e-4b02-a9c1-6580f9388430/70-3
00:09:10.178 --> 00:09:15.068
<v Tom Kerrigan>So there's a lot more of them around. They can boost your yield.</v>

19c47ec4-e17e-4b02-a9c1-6580f9388430/70-4
00:09:15.068 --> 00:09:21.839
<v Tom Kerrigan>But they cost more to buy, they've got two lots of maintenance, and sometimes resale's a bit trickier,</v>

19c47ec4-e17e-4b02-a9c1-6580f9388430/70-5
00:09:21.839 --> 00:09:28.610
<v Tom Kerrigan>because a lot of owner-occupier buyers don't want them. So it's not a no, it's just a trade-off.</v>

8f9bacb4-efcd-4a3e-92e4-c3feb0b300b9/71-0
00:09:29.044 --> 00:09:29.754
<v Callum P (Guest)>Hmm.</v>

19c47ec4-e17e-4b02-a9c1-6580f9388430/72-0
00:09:30.009 --> 00:09:32.783
<v Tom Kerrigan>What I'd suggest is, let's look at both.</v>

19c47ec4-e17e-4b02-a9c1-6580f9388430/72-1
00:09:32.783 --> 00:09:39.026
<v Tom Kerrigan>I'll put it as a "would consider" in the brief, but our main target is a straightforward house,</v>

19c47ec4-e17e-4b02-a9c1-6580f9388430/72-2
00:09:39.026 --> 00:09:41.800
<v Tom Kerrigan>three or four bedrooms, on a good block.</v>

19c47ec4-e17e-4b02-a9c1-6580f9388430/72-3
00:09:41.800 --> 00:09:46.308
<v Tom Kerrigan>And if a good dual income one comes up in the right spot,</v>

19c47ec4-e17e-4b02-a9c1-6580f9388430/72-4
00:09:46.308 --> 00:09:50.470
<v Tom Kerrigan>I'll show you and we can run the numbers side by side.</v>

c21b6ccb-ea74-4225-8514-3495a0233a54/73-0
00:09:51.346 --> 00:09:54.295
<v Anh Tran (Guest)>Okay. That's fine. I can live with that.</v>

8f9bacb4-efcd-4a3e-92e4-c3feb0b300b9/74-0
00:09:55.065 --> 00:09:56.340
<v Callum P (Guest)>Yeah. That's good.</v>

7801aafa-82a9-499c-932d-80207849fbb9/75-0
00:09:56.846 --> 00:09:59.701
<v Anh Tran (Guest)>Oh, sorry, that's—she's awake. Callum, can you—</v>

0d3d64fb-898e-4262-a608-3cae34d611b3/76-0
00:09:59.828 --> 00:10:04.821
<v Callum P (Guest)>Yep, I'll grab her. Keep going, I can hear you from the hallway.</v>

19c47ec4-e17e-4b02-a9c1-6580f9388430/77-0
00:10:05.081 --> 00:10:08.436
<v Tom Kerrigan>No stress. How old did you say, two?</v>

7801aafa-82a9-499c-932d-80207849fbb9/78-0
00:10:09.227 --> 00:10:14.875
<v Anh Tran (Guest)>Two in January. She's been sick, so she's been napping at weird times. Sorry.</v>

19c47ec4-e17e-4b02-a9c1-6580f9388430/79-0
00:10:15.327 --> 00:10:21.255
<v Tom Kerrigan>Don't apologise, I've got a four year old, I've done plenty of calls with a kid on my</v>

19c47ec4-e17e-4b02-a9c1-6580f9388430/79-1
00:10:21.255 --> 00:10:27.184
<v Tom Kerrigan>lap. Okay, so while Callum's wrangling her, can I ask you, Anh, what's your biggest worry with this?</v>

19c47ec4-e17e-4b02-a9c1-6580f9388430/79-2
00:10:27.184 --> 00:10:30.478
<v Tom Kerrigan>Like, the thing that would keep you up at night.</v>

7801aafa-82a9-499c-932d-80207849fbb9/80-0
00:10:31.501 --> 00:10:36.936
<v Anh Tran (Guest)>Um. Honestly? Buying something we've never seen, in a city we don't really know,</v>

7801aafa-82a9-499c-932d-80207849fbb9/80-1
00:10:36.936 --> 00:10:40.430
<v Anh Tran (Guest)>and then it turns out to be a dud.</v>

7801aafa-82a9-499c-932d-80207849fbb9/80-2
00:10:40.430 --> 00:10:46.642
<v Anh Tran (Guest)>Like, it's got some massive problem and we're stuck with it. And the tenants trash it.</v>

e166af7f-8796-4036-bd60-8f8d4df4c5d7/81-0
00:10:47.243 --> 00:10:51.379
<v Tom Kerrigan>Yeah. That's the most common one. And it's a fair worry.</v>

e166af7f-8796-4036-bd60-8f8d4df4c5d7/81-1
00:10:51.379 --> 00:10:55.516
<v Tom Kerrigan>That's most of what I'm there to stop, to be honest.</v>

0d3d64fb-898e-4262-a608-3cae34d611b3/82-0
00:10:56.160 --> 00:11:01.658
<v Callum P (Guest)>Okay, I'm back. She's got her bunny and some crackers. We've got maybe ten minutes.</v>

e166af7f-8796-4036-bd60-8f8d4df4c5d7/83-0
00:11:02.661 --> 00:11:04.623
<v Tom Kerrigan>Ha. Let's go fast then.</v>

e166af7f-8796-4036-bd60-8f8d4df4c5d7/84-0
00:11:05.493 --> 00:11:09.241
<v Tom Kerrigan>Okay. And the house. What era? Any preferences on that?</v>

0d3d64fb-898e-4262-a608-3cae34d611b3/85-0
00:11:09.899 --> 00:11:12.863
<v Callum P (Guest)>I don't really know. What would you recommend?</v>

583bdc77-76c7-40c9-b54b-b5c3d0253ec5/86-0
00:11:13.428 --> 00:11:20.006
<v Tom Kerrigan>So, for investors on a budget like yours, I generally like houses from the seventies through to the</v>

583bdc77-76c7-40c9-b54b-b5c3d0253ec5/86-1
00:11:20.006 --> 00:11:24.391
<v Tom Kerrigan>two thousands. Brick, or brick veneer, with a tile or metal roof.</v>

583bdc77-76c7-40c9-b54b-b5c3d0253ec5/86-2
00:11:24.391 --> 00:11:29.507
<v Tom Kerrigan>They're solid, they're low maintenance, they're usually on bigger blocks than the newer stuff.</v>

583bdc77-76c7-40c9-b54b-b5c3d0253ec5/86-3
00:11:29.507 --> 00:11:34.622
<v Tom Kerrigan>Some of the older timber houses are fine too, but they need more maintenance,</v>

583bdc77-76c7-40c9-b54b-b5c3d0253ec5/86-4
00:11:34.622 --> 00:11:37.911
<v Tom Kerrigan>and you've got to watch for termites and stumps.</v>

7801aafa-82a9-499c-932d-80207849fbb9/87-0
00:11:38.711 --> 00:11:41.503
<v Anh Tran (Guest)>Termites. I didn't even think about termites.</v>

292773b6-7b74-4f03-b334-e59ed9a7ef3f/88-0
00:11:42.203 --> 00:11:48.214
<v Tom Kerrigan>Yeah, in Queensland, it's a real thing. That's why the building and pest is so important.</v>

292773b6-7b74-4f03-b334-e59ed9a7ef3f/88-1
00:11:48.214 --> 00:11:52.347
<v Tom Kerrigan>And I'll check if there's a termite management system in place.</v>

292773b6-7b74-4f03-b334-e59ed9a7ef3f/88-2
00:11:52.347 --> 00:11:57.983
<v Tom Kerrigan>Some older houses need a bit of work to get compliant for rentals now too,</v>

292773b6-7b74-4f03-b334-e59ed9a7ef3f/88-3
00:11:57.983 --> 00:12:00.988
<v Tom Kerrigan>with the minimum housing standards that came in.</v>

292773b6-7b74-4f03-b334-e59ed9a7ef3f/88-4
00:12:00.988 --> 00:12:07.751
<v Tom Kerrigan>And smoke alarms, every house in Queensland needs the interconnected photoelectric ones by the start of next year,</v>

292773b6-7b74-4f03-b334-e59ed9a7ef3f/88-5
00:12:07.751 --> 00:12:10.381
<v Tom Kerrigan>and rentals already have to have them.</v>

292773b6-7b74-4f03-b334-e59ed9a7ef3f/88-6
00:12:10.381 --> 00:12:17.144
<v Tom Kerrigan>So that's something I'll check, because it can be a couple of thousand to fix if they're not</v>

292773b6-7b74-4f03-b334-e59ed9a7ef3f/88-7
00:12:17.144 --> 00:12:17.519
<v Tom Kerrigan>there.</v>

0d3d64fb-898e-4262-a608-3cae34d611b3/89-0
00:12:19.933 --> 00:12:23.179
<v Callum P (Guest)>Okay. That's a lot of stuff to know.</v>

292773b6-7b74-4f03-b334-e59ed9a7ef3f/90-0
00:12:23.824 --> 00:12:29.569
<v Tom Kerrigan>Ha. That's what I'm for. Okay, so, rent. What kind of rent are you hoping for?</v>

0d3d64fb-898e-4262-a608-3cae34d611b3/91-0
00:12:29.991 --> 00:12:33.858
<v Callum P (Guest)>I was hoping, like, six hundred a week? Is that realistic?</v>

292773b6-7b74-4f03-b334-e59ed9a7ef3f/92-0
00:12:34.390 --> 00:12:37.882
<v Tom Kerrigan>For a four bed house in most of those suburbs, yeah,</v>

292773b6-7b74-4f03-b334-e59ed9a7ef3f/92-1
00:12:37.882 --> 00:12:41.057
<v Tom Kerrigan>five-eighty to six-fifty a week is realistic at the moment.</v>

292773b6-7b74-4f03-b334-e59ed9a7ef3f/92-2
00:12:41.057 --> 00:12:43.914
<v Tom Kerrigan>Three bed, a bit less, maybe five-twenty to five-eighty.</v>

292773b6-7b74-4f03-b334-e59ed9a7ef3f/92-3
00:12:43.914 --> 00:12:47.724
<v Tom Kerrigan>So on an eight hundred thousand house, at six hundred a week,</v>

292773b6-7b74-4f03-b334-e59ed9a7ef3f/92-4
00:12:47.724 --> 00:12:51.851
<v Tom Kerrigan>you're looking at a yield of about three point nine percent, before costs.</v>

0d3d64fb-898e-4262-a608-3cae34d611b3/93-0
00:12:52.244 --> 00:12:53.037
<v Callum P (Guest)>Okay.</v>

7801aafa-82a9-499c-932d-80207849fbb9/94-0
00:12:53.743 --> 00:12:56.811
<v Anh Tran (Guest)>So would it be, like, negatively geared?</v>

895aad07-399e-4624-9f90-2d4c978945d4/95-0
00:12:57.289 --> 00:12:59.830
<v Tom Kerrigan>Probably a bit, yes, at today's rates.</v>

895aad07-399e-4624-9f90-2d4c978945d4/95-1
00:12:59.830 --> 00:13:04.185
<v Tom Kerrigan>It depends on your loan and your interest rate and all that.</v>

895aad07-399e-4624-9f90-2d4c978945d4/95-2
00:13:04.185 --> 00:13:07.452
<v Tom Kerrigan>That's really one for your accountant and your broker.</v>

895aad07-399e-4624-9f90-2d4c978945d4/95-3
00:13:07.452 --> 00:13:11.807
<v Tom Kerrigan>I can give you the rent and the costs on each property,</v>

895aad07-399e-4624-9f90-2d4c978945d4/95-4
00:13:11.807 --> 00:13:15.800
<v Tom Kerrigan>but how it works with your tax, I'd talk to them.</v>

aaa1a370-c132-40fa-b313-1487e117a642/96-0
00:13:16.074 --> 00:13:22.082
<v Anh Tran (Guest)>Yeah. We've got an accountant. He's been asking us about, like, how we buy it. Whose name.</v>

895aad07-399e-4624-9f90-2d4c978945d4/97-0
00:13:22.857 --> 00:13:27.867
<v Tom Kerrigan>Yeah, that's a really important question, and it's one to sort out before we buy anything,</v>

895aad07-399e-4624-9f90-2d4c978945d4/97-1
00:13:27.867 --> 00:13:33.503
<v Tom Kerrigan>because once the contract's signed, it's hard to change the buyer. So talk to him about that soon.</v>

895aad07-399e-4624-9f90-2d4c978945d4/97-2
00:13:33.503 --> 00:13:34.756
<v Tom Kerrigan>Same with land tax.</v>

895aad07-399e-4624-9f90-2d4c978945d4/97-3
00:13:34.756 --> 00:13:40.079
<v Tom Kerrigan>In Queensland, there's a threshold, and for one property at your price point you're often under it,</v>

895aad07-399e-4624-9f90-2d4c978945d4/97-4
00:13:40.079 --> 00:13:41.331
<v Tom Kerrigan>but he should check.</v>

0d3d64fb-898e-4262-a608-3cae34d611b3/98-0
00:13:41.618 --> 00:13:43.909
<v Callum P (Guest)>Okay. I'll email him tomorrow.</v>

895aad07-399e-4624-9f90-2d4c978945d4/99-0
00:13:44.191 --> 00:13:47.696
<v Tom Kerrigan>Great. Okay, so property management. Have you thought about that?</v>

0d3d64fb-898e-4262-a608-3cae34d611b3/100-0
00:13:48.247 --> 00:13:51.748
<v Callum P (Guest)>Not really. We figured we'd find someone once we buy.</v>

895aad07-399e-4624-9f90-2d4c978945d4/101-0
00:13:52.418 --> 00:13:53.567
<v Tom Kerrigan>Yeah, that's fine.</v>

895aad07-399e-4624-9f90-2d4c978945d4/101-1
00:13:53.567 --> 00:14:00.463
<v Tom Kerrigan>I can introduce you to a couple of property managers in whichever area we end up buying in.</v>

895aad07-399e-4624-9f90-2d4c978945d4/101-2
00:14:00.463 --> 00:14:04.677
<v Tom Kerrigan>I don't get anything from them, I just know who's good.</v>

895aad07-399e-4624-9f90-2d4c978945d4/101-3
00:14:04.677 --> 00:14:11.573
<v Tom Kerrigan>And a good property manager makes a massive difference with an interstate investment. They're your eyes and ears.</v>

aaa1a370-c132-40fa-b313-1487e117a642/102-0
00:14:11.869 --> 00:14:12.908
<v Anh Tran (Guest)>That's good.</v>

895aad07-399e-4624-9f90-2d4c978945d4/103-0
00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:19.920
<v Tom Kerrigan>And then, do you want a property with a tenant already in, or vacant?</v>

0d3d64fb-898e-4262-a608-3cae34d611b3/104-0
00:14:20.324 --> 00:14:21.812
<v Callum P (Guest)>Um, does it matter?</v>

d0b9d29d-ee4c-4e76-86ed-84feb105c8a3/105-0
00:14:22.254 --> 00:14:26.373
<v Tom Kerrigan>It can. A tenanted property means you've got rent from day one.</v>

d0b9d29d-ee4c-4e76-86ed-84feb105c8a3/105-1
