<v Tom Kerrigan>you're stuck with it for a while, because in Queensland you can only increase the rent once every</v>

d0b9d29d-ee4c-4e76-86ed-84feb105c8a3/105-3
00:14:37.357 --> 00:14:41.133
<v Tom Kerrigan>twelve months, and that's tied to the property, not the tenant.</v>

d0b9d29d-ee4c-4e76-86ed-84feb105c8a3/105-4
00:14:41.133 --> 00:14:44.566
<v Tom Kerrigan>So I'd check the lease, the rent, the rental history.</v>

d0b9d29d-ee4c-4e76-86ed-84feb105c8a3/105-5
00:14:44.566 --> 00:14:48.342
<v Tom Kerrigan>Vacant means you can pick your tenant and set the rent,</v>

d0b9d29d-ee4c-4e76-86ed-84feb105c8a3/105-6
00:14:48.342 --> 00:14:51.431
<v Tom Kerrigan>but you might have a few weeks without rent.</v>

aaa1a370-c132-40fa-b313-1487e117a642/106-0
00:14:51.732 --> 00:14:54.875
<v Anh Tran (Guest)>Okay. I guess either is fine, depending.</v>

d0b9d29d-ee4c-4e76-86ed-84feb105c8a3/107-0
00:14:55.676 --> 00:14:59.961
<v Tom Kerrigan>Yep, depending. Okay, and timing. Is there a timeframe you're working to?</v>

0d3d64fb-898e-4262-a608-3cae34d611b3/108-0
00:15:00.942 --> 00:15:05.227
<v Callum P (Guest)>Um, not really. Like, we'd like to buy in the next few months.</v>

0d3d64fb-898e-4262-a608-3cae34d611b3/108-1
00:15:05.227 --> 00:15:08.523
<v Callum P (Guest)>Before the end of the financial year would be good.</v>

aaa1a370-c132-40fa-b313-1487e117a642/109-0
00:15:09.084 --> 00:15:14.035
<v Anh Tran (Guest)>I'd like to get it done before I go back to work in March, honestly.</v>

aaa1a370-c132-40fa-b313-1487e117a642/109-1
00:15:14.035 --> 00:15:15.685
<v Anh Tran (Guest)>So I'm not juggling it.</v>

0d3d64fb-898e-4262-a608-3cae34d611b3/110-0
00:15:16.462 --> 00:15:17.848
<v Callum P (Guest)>Okay, March then.</v>

b84f2d9a-6dd7-4300-845e-405e08e13c71/111-0
00:15:18.589 --> 00:15:21.096
<v Tom Kerrigan>Okay, that's a nice amount of time.</v>

b84f2d9a-6dd7-4300-845e-405e08e13c71/111-1
00:15:21.096 --> 00:15:25.394
<v Tom Kerrigan>And look, I'll be honest, the Christmas period's usually a bit slower,</v>

b84f2d9a-6dd7-4300-845e-405e08e13c71/111-2
00:15:25.394 --> 00:15:30.051
<v Tom Kerrigan>but there's often good opportunities in December and January, because there's less competition.</v>

b84f2d9a-6dd7-4300-845e-405e08e13c71/111-3
00:15:30.051 --> 00:15:33.632
<v Tom Kerrigan>And the end of January, February, things pick up again.</v>

b84f2d9a-6dd7-4300-845e-405e08e13c71/111-4
00:15:33.632 --> 00:15:39.363
<v Tom Kerrigan>So if we start now, that gives us two, three months to find the right one.</v>

b84f2d9a-6dd7-4300-845e-405e08e13c71/111-5
00:15:39.363 --> 00:15:40.438
<v Tom Kerrigan>Which is plenty.</v>

0d3d64fb-898e-4262-a608-3cae34d611b3/112-0
00:15:41.294 --> 00:15:42.373
<v Callum P (Guest)>Okay. Good.</v>

b84f2d9a-6dd7-4300-845e-405e08e13c71/113-0
00:15:44.572 --> 00:15:48.850
<v Tom Kerrigan>Okay, and the other thing, how do you want to be involved?</v>

b84f2d9a-6dd7-4300-845e-405e08e13c71/113-1
00:15:48.850 --> 00:15:55.268
